From: BearddOddity <beardedoddity@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:00:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] Beardd's Wayfarer: floors, region-map waypoints, quest
 people, player keys, the compass in the trail's colour

The guide trail leads between a dungeon's floors over the way the player's map knows (world.known(): the walked cells,
stacked climbs, one-way teleporters and drops), and to the nearest reachable cell where it cannot reach the mark. Pins
keep a place on its own floor (mapPick's sixth argument, dyMetres; retarget's [x, z, y]), pin the exit on the floor the
player came in on, survive a teleporter's jump and the open world's tile step, and lead to the region map's followed
waypoints outdoors (world.waypoints()). The waypoint diamond stays on its spot and waits on the screen's edge the way the
mark lies; it colours a region waypoint vermilion.

Quest guidance follows the journal: an entry that says where a person waits points at their building or town
(questLens personSiteOf), a person the quest is done with is marked no more and is no place to go (questGuidance
personDealtWith), and a town the entry names but the map lacks is ringed on the region map (`seek`).

Every module key is the player's (Shift+F1, src/mods/keysPanel.js; the panel's words in every locale). A module may colour
the compass's mark (dfo.markColour); the guide trail gives it its look's colour while it is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
